<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="ram-egg" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Ramen Egg</title>

  <p>
    Ingredients
  </p>
  <tabular>
    <row>
      <cell><term>Marinade</term></cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{3}{4}</m> cup mirin</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{4}</m> cup soy sauce</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
    <cell><m>\frac{1}{4}</m> cup dark soy sauce</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> cup water (if marinating longer than 6 hours)</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><term>Spices (optional)</term></cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> teaspoon cayenne pepper</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 cloves garlic</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 star anise</cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>

  <p>Instructions
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          Bring eggs to a boil.  Remove from heat, and let sit 10 minutes.  Put in cold water until cool.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Meanwhile, put marinade ingredients in a tall container with airtight lid.  Whisk to combine.  If adding additional spices, bring marinade just to simmer in a small saucepan with spices.  Remove from heat and let it cool to room temperature.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Peel eggs and place in marinade in the tall airtight container.  Add <m>\frac{1}{2}</m> cup water if marinating longer than 6 hours.  Let sit for 2 to 24 hours.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Remove eggs from marinade and place in an airtight container.  Store for up to 5 days.  Marinade can be stored in airtight container for up to 3 weeks.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>

  <p>
    Notes:
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          You can substitute regular soy sauce for dark soy sauce if you do not have a full range of soy sauces.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Used in <xref ref="ramen-sh">Ramen (Shoyu)</xref>
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</section>